  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116370",
      "title": "Introducing HTTP Response Interceptors",
      "lectureOrder": 240,
      "videoOrder": 228,
      "sourceHash": "6197e54ee3dff9792589be7788298d92b1f5d195e9fc7a690f885c7bc2e9def4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 2.76,
          "en": "Now besides adding an interceptor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.76,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "that intercepts outgoing requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 8.13,
          "en": "you can also build up on that interceptor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.13,
          "end": 10.893,
          "en": "to also intercept incoming responses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.85,
          "end": 15.3,
          "en": "Now for that, you'll always need such a request interceptor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.3,
          "end": 18.81,
          "en": "because it's then the result of calling next down here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.81,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "which will allow you to also intercept responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 25.02,
          "en": "and act on responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.02,
          "end": 27.87,
          "en": "because next will give you an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.87,
          "end": 31.773,
          "en": "that's wrapped around an HTTP event type of value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.12,
          "end": 35.19,
          "en": "And you can therefore call pipe here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.19,
          "end": 39.993,
          "en": "since it's an observable to change it or to tap into it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.95,
          "end": 42.81,
          "en": "We don't wanna subscribe here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.81,
          "end": 45.63,
          "en": "because that would be the end of this observable chain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.63,
          "end": 48.99,
          "en": "and other parts in the application now wouldn't be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.99,
          "end": 51.96,
          "en": "to interact with that response anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.96,
          "end": 53.703,
          "en": "So pipe it is instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 56.58,
          "en": "And to pipe you can now pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.58,
          "end": 58.653,
          "en": "all the operators you learned about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.52,
          "end": 63.21,
          "en": "For example, tap to define your own observer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.21,
          "end": 65.17,
          "en": "that will execute your own code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.45,
          "end": 70.71000000000001,
          "en": "and here I'll simply wait for the next value to be emitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.71000000000001,
          "end": 73.18,
          "en": "which here will actually be of type event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.73,
          "end": 79.02,
          "en": "because here will actually get an event type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.02,
          "end": 81.3,
          "en": "instead of the response data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.3,
          "end": 86.3,
          "en": "But this event value actually will have a type field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.31,
          "end": 90.63,
          "en": "which we can use in a if check to check if the event type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.63,
          "end": 95.63,
          "en": "is HTTP event type, which must be imported from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.5,
          "end": 100.413,
          "en": "at Angular common http.response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.45,
          "end": 107.85,
          "en": "And as you see, there are other kinds of events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.85,
          "end": 109.35,
          "en": "that could be emitted as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.03,
          "end": 114.39,
          "en": "For example, if a request was just sent, if you wanted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.39,
          "end": 117.96000000000001,
          "en": "to listen to that and execute code, you could do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 117.96000000000001,
          "end": 119.58,
          "en": "with the sent event type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.58,
          "end": 121.56,
          "en": "But here I'm interested if the event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.56,
          "end": 124.23,
          "en": "that was in the end emitted by this observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.23,
          "end": 127.77,
          "en": "is of type response, which means we're dealing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.77,
          "end": 129.72,
          "en": "with the response here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.72,
          "end": 134.44,
          "en": "And in that case, I'll simply log incoming response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.42,
          "end": 140.42000000000002,
          "en": "and then log event status and maybe also the body like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 146.43,
          "end": 148.59,
          "en": "which will be the response status code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 148.59,
          "end": 150.183,
          "en": "and the response body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 151.11,
          "end": 154.233,
          "en": "And that's how you can set up a response interceptor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 155.73,
          "end": 159,
          "en": "With that done, if you reload, you got some logs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 159,
          "end": 162.84,
          "en": "for example, the incoming response log, the status code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 162.84,
          "end": 164.43,
          "en": "and then the response body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 164.43,
          "end": 166.713,
          "en": "which is of course this array of places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 168.51,
          "end": 170.22,
          "en": "In this case of the user places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 172.833,
          "en": "because that was the first response to arrive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.24,
          "end": 176.13,
          "en": "And that's therefore how you can register",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 176.13,
          "end": 179.04,
          "en": "such response interceptors in combination",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 179.04,
          "end": 181.083,
          "en": "with request interceptors.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
